## 1. API Endpoint Reference

### API #70 — Add Single Round Result

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| **Method** | `POST` |
| **URL** | `/api/college/add_round_result/:roundId` |
| **Auth** | Bearer Token (COLLEGEADMIN or TPO) |

#### Request Body

```json
{
  "application_id": "a1b2c3d4-....",
  "result_status": "passed",
  "score": 85.50,
  "remarks": "Strong performance in coding round",
  "attended": true,
  "scheduled_at": "2026-03-05T10:00:00.000Z",
  "completed_at": "2026-03-05T11:30:00.000Z"
}
```

| Field | Type | Required | Validation |
|-------|------|----------|------------|
| `application_id` | UUID | ✅ | Must belong to the round's job and college |
| `result_status` | string | ❌ | `pending` (default), `passed`, `failed`, `on_hold`, `absent` |
| `score` | number | ❌ | 0–100000, 2 decimal places |
| `remarks` | string | ❌ | max 2000 chars |
| `attended` | boolean | ❌ | defaults to false |
| `scheduled_at` | ISO datetime | ❌ | When the student is scheduled |
| `completed_at` | ISO datetime | ❌ | Must be after `scheduled_at` |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The API auto-resolves `student_id` from the `application_id`. You only need to provide the `application_id`.
> Duplicate check: UNIQUE on [(application_id, round_id)](file:///c:/Users/Gopal%20Bharat%20Patil/OneDrive/Desktop/placement-crm-api/src/config/db.js#61-97) — use Update API for existing results.

#### Success Response (201)

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Round result added successfully",
  "data": {
    "result_id": "...",
    "application_id": "...",
    "round_id": "...",
    "student_id": "...",
    "result_status": "passed",
    "score": 85.50,
    "remarks": "Strong performance",
    "attended": true,
    "scheduled_at": "2026-03-05T10:00:00.000Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-03-05T11:30:00.000Z",
    "student_name": "Rahul Sharma",
    "student_email": "rahul@email.com",
    "round_name": "Coding Test",
    "round_number": 1,
    "job_title": "Software Developer",
    "company_name": "TCS"
  }
}
```

